      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Food craving refers to an intense desire to consume a specific food. The Food Cravings Questionnaires (FCQs) assess food cravings on a trait and a state level."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHOD",
          "content": "The current study examined half-year retest-reliability of the Food Cravings Questionnaire-Trait-reduced (FCQ-T-r) and the Food Cravings Questionnaire-State (FCQ-S) and reports associations with current food deprivation in female students."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The FCQ-T-r had higher retest-reliability (r tt\u2009=\u2009.74) than the FCQ-S (r tt\u2009=\u2009.39). Although trait food craving was correlated with state food craving, it was unaffected by current food deprivation."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Although state and trait food craving are interdependent, the FCQs are able to differentiate between the two. As scores of the FCQ-T-r represent a stable trait, but are also sensitive to changes in eating behavior, they may be useful for the investigation of the course of eating disorders and obesity."
        }
      ]},
